## 7. Implementation Roadmap

* [ ] **Phase 1: Environment & Finance Setup**
  * Stand up the cloud container host + SQLite-on-volume; put **Cloudflare Access (Google SSO + family allowlist)** in front.
  * Stand up the home-side **Cloudflare Tunnel** agent (initially just for Home Assistant reachability).
  * Deploy Actual Budget and build a worker to pull and cache budget balances.
* [ ] **Phase 2: Meal & Cart Core**
  * Port over the existing vibe-coded meal planner scripts into the Hub backend.
  * Expose an endpoint that outputs the unified grocery list.
  * Solidify the Playwright automation script to pipe lists to the Whole Foods cart.
* [ ] **Phase 3: The Rich Web UI**
  * Build the mobile/desktop responsive views for scheduling meals and editing tasks.
  * Wire up the unified feed per §2.6: Google Calendar mirrored read-only; Tasks/chores as a Household-OS-owned surface (not Google Tasks); Keep out of scope.
* [ ] **Phase 4: E-Ink Frontend Implementation**
  * Design an e-ink-optimized CSS media query/route layout.
  * Set up the server-side screenshot generation worker.
  * Configure hardware touch boundaries to map to the rating and check-off API endpoints.
  * Provision the panel's narrow device token (see §4.3).

